# Commit message template — conventional commits only.
# Activate:  git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# Format:
#   <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
#   <body: what + why, wrapped at 100 chars>
#
#   <footer: refs, breaking changes>
#
# Types:
#   feat      new capability
#   fix       bug fix
#   refactor  no behaviour change
#   perf      performance improvement
#   test      tests only
#   docs      documentation only
#   build     packaging / dependencies / containers
#   ci        CI/CD pipelines
#   chore     tooling, hygiene, non-functional
#   revert    revert a commit
#
# Scopes: core, config, models, data, sampling, training, evaluation,
#         agent, serving, cli, api, worker, k8s, docker, tf, docs, repo
#
# Examples:
#   feat(serving): add continuous batching to inference engine
#   fix(diffusion): clamp posterior variance to avoid log(0)
#   docs(arch): add failure-mode analysis for the queue layer
#   BREAKING CHANGE: api now requires X-API-Key on every route
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# <type>(<scope>): <subject, imperative, <=72 chars>
